WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.199
At the microtome, a useful zebrafish section never

00:00:04.199 --> 00:00:07.479
emerged. The photographed fragments are the actual

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:07.947
outcome.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.741
To cut a useful section of a zebrafish specimen,

00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:22.602
orientation and compatible embedding materials must

00:00:22.602 --> 00:00:23.556
work together.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:34.631
The specimen was oriented in an agarose pre-embedding

00:00:34.631 --> 00:00:37.767
support before subsequent paraffin processing. The

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.903
hoped-for geometry depended on their compatibility.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.152
Agarose and paraffin did not form the coherent

00:00:50.152 --> 00:00:52.465
embedding system the microtome needed.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:05.355
Material separation frustrated sectioning. There was no

00:01:05.355 --> 00:01:08.703
interpretable histological slice from that attempt.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.251
Agarose oriented the specimen; paraffin was intended to

00:01:20.251 --> 00:01:23.577
support cutting. Their separation suggests a materials

00:01:23.577 --> 00:01:26.903
problem but does not prove its mechanism.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:37.175
The images identify an upstream materials bottleneck. A

00:01:37.175 --> 00:01:41.309
changed processing protocol needs its own experimental

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:41.900
verification.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.715
A failed preparation deserves an accurate record and a

00:01:50.715 --> 00:01:54.033
redesigned experiment, not an animated happy ending.
